      "title": "Make range_t.ranges a flexible array member.",
      "message": "Make range_t.ranges a flexible array member.\n\nGCC's static analyzer somehow gets confused by the size computations around\nRANGE_HDR_SIZE and complains about a nonexistent array-bounds overrun when\nusing __attribute__((alloc_size(n))) to validate bounds of some\ndynamically-allocated buffers.\n\nSwitching to a flexible array member addresses the problem.\n\nThe initialization of default packet-size ranges in the stats_tree is rewritten\nto use the public range API so as to avoid problems with initializing\nstructures containing flexible array members.\n",
      "author_name": "Darius Davis",
      "author_email": "darius-wireshark@free-range.com.au",
      "authored_date": "2024-06-12T15:03:48.000+10:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
